The more gifts you get, the less likely you are to get the next gift;
and "fully random" means "fully random".  There is no proscription
against getting another ordinary helmet if you already have a helmet; 
nor is there a proscription against getting an orcish cloak, possibly
the worst piece of armor available (except for orcs).

Also, there is a not-insignificant chance that you'll get a weapon,
which does very little to enhance your AC -- and if you think orcish
cloaks can become redundant, how about the fourth knife?

The well never completely dries up, but the point I'm getting at is that
a random fount of giftitude is going to give you some really cool things
sometimes, and, well, some stuff you aren't really sure you wanted other
times.  (The recently-mentioned javelin is a good example.)

Finally, all of this largesse is subject to there being a coaligned altar 
available, and arranging this before XL4 can be very tricky.  This
feature is far from set in stone at the moment (it's trivial to make
everything out of the hopper be +3, for example), but as with some of my 
other changes, it looks a lot more broken at first glance than it actually is.

(With regard to "allowing the player to get a full set of +5 armor"... 
you mean players didn't routinely wish up markers at the Castle and make
that anyway, except with their custom "finish the game" armor instead of
a bunch of random glop from god?  ;)

